  Timbre Watermarking      GPL-3.0. Hard block. Not read, not used.

Reimplemented from published descriptions, with no third-party code consulted line by line:

  - the image-source method (Allen & Berkley 1979) and Eyring's reverberation formula, in
    src/genomark_n/rir/image_source.py;
  - the Schroeder spreading function / half-Bark masking model, ported from this repository's own
    crates/audio-provenance-bench/src/perceptual.rs (Apache-2.0, same project) into
    src/genomark_n/perceptual.py;
  - RBJ audio-EQ-cookbook biquad coefficients, in src/genomark_n/distortion/dsp.py;
  - CRC-24/OPENPGP, in src/genomark_n/payload.py, verified against the standard check value
    crc24(b"123456789") == 0x21CF02.

DATA. No corpus is bundled. Loaders refuse any manifest entry whose declared licence is outside
{CC0-1.0, CC-BY-*, CC-BY-SA-*, audio-provenance-owned, audio-provenance-licensed, public-domain} and refuse the
following sources by name, with the reason, in src/genomark_n/data/licences.py:

  unfiltered FMA           metadata is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0; audio licences are heterogeneous per track
                           and a substantial fraction are NonCommercial (spec 9.1)
  OpenSLR-28 RIRS_NOISES   16 kHz only; driving a 48 kHz layer with it fabricates the 8-24 kHz band
                           where transducer roll-off lives (spec 9.2)
  Aachen AIR standalone    research use only (spec 9.2)

Runtime dependencies are declared in pyproject.toml and are installed from PyPI; their licences are
their own and none of their source is copied into this tree.

This directory is part of audio-provenance-sdk and is Apache-2.0, matching the workspace.
